<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis, Grand Condé</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1621">1621</a>–<a href="/years/1686">1686</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Great Condé, Louis II de Bourbon, Prince of Condé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis, Grand Condé, born Louis II de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> and Prince of Condé from 1646, was one of the leading French generals of the seventeenth century. As the young Duke of Enghien he destroyed the Spanish army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rocroi">Rocroi</a> in 1643, and he won further victories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. He rebelled during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-fronde">Fronde</a> and fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in the 1650s, but was pardoned in 1659 and served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> again.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-grand-conde.jpg" alt="Louis, Grand Condé" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Justus van Egmont · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis,_Grand_Cond%C3%A9.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
